                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation(2)/65: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-27T19:00:00-04:00">June 27, 1940—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>120. Your 168, June 24, 2 p.m. Please assure the Minister of Foreign Affairs on
                    my behalf and on that of the Under Secretary that his constructive interest in
                    the success of the proposed meeting at Habana is sincerely appreciated here.</p>
                <p>The status of the agenda for the meeting is described in the Department’s
                    circular telegram of June 24, 1 p.m. The Department hopes that it will be
                    possible prior to the meeting to exchange views regarding certain specific
                    proposals along economic lines which are now being worked out. In this
                    connection any expression on the part of the Colombian Government would be
                    highly welcome.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
